There are a couple of answers to this:

1) Play an elf, and reach level 4, where you get sleep resistance
automatically.  Or play a monk , who automatically gets sleep
resistance at level 1.

Both have their disadvantages, of course.  Elves have their strength
capped at 18 and are always chaotic.   Monks can't wear body armor
until they are very high experience, when high experience and luck
counterbalances the -20 to-hit penalty.

Of just keep eating corpses and hope for the best next time :)

2)  Get reflection , ASAP.

That will solve not just this problem but your wand of cold, wand of
fire, wand of magic missile, dragon breath, winter wolf breath
problems.  I like the amulet  best, but there's also the shield of
reflection or silver dragon scale armor.

If you don't have reflection there are a few things you can do which
will
mitigate, but not totally prevent, this problem.


-- invisibility or displacement.  Makes it harder to hit you. Get to
melee range,I *think* the likelihood of using wands decreases
dramatically. Of course, getting in melee has it's own set of
problems...

But invisibility in particular is fairly easy to get.  Try on every
uncursed ring you find ... rings of invisibility seem rather common.

-- fun with polearms.
A polearm advanced to 'skilled' can hit anything within 2 squares,
including
not in a direct line.

That's how I killed a black dragon a few games ago. I walk into a
throne room, and there's an adult black dragon there. I'm afraid of
it's disintegration ray, but I have a polearm, and stealth ... so
here's what I do.

Here's the setup.

------
.....@.|
.....MM|
.... MD|
---------

where @ is me, D is the black dragon, and "M" are three asleep
monsters.
I pull out my polearm at this point and simply stab the dragon to
death. he
can't move, because he's blocked by the monsters and the dungeon
wall.
He can't melee, because I'm not in melee range.  Nor can he hit me
with his breath weapon, because I'm not in direct line of fire (I'm a
knight's move away, 2 up and one left).  OTOH, I can hit him with my
polearm, and I do so repeatedly.  Whack whack whack he's dead. Melee
through the M, eat the black dragon corpse, now I'm disintegration
resistant.

Of course, one has to build up polearm skill to do this, and everyone
starts out unskilled. Not to worry!  Mimics in shops make perfect
polearm bait. They're slow, so you can outrun them, leading them a
merry chase around the shop while stabbing them repeatedly from 2
squares away.

This implies, of course, that you are playing a class that can reach
skilled or expert in polearms.

>o I try to avoid
any monster who could have a wand of sleep before I get sleep
resistance?

How?  Any monster with hands that is not mindless can use a wand.
That means werejackals, wererats, werewolves, gnomes, gnome lords,
gnome wizards, gnome kings, kobolds, large kobolds, kobold shamans,
kobold lords, goblins, mordor orcs, uruk-hai, soldiers, woodland
elves, green elves,...

The only real solution to this is : Have reflection, or get to the
wands first.
Typically, these wands are lying loose in the dungeon and are later
picked up, so if you do a fast sweep of a level you *might* be able to
pick it up
before someone else does.  Then see how your enemies like wands of
sleep!

